Build and run:
Requires gcc, make and the CUnit library (-lcunit) and optionally valgrind to build and run


make            # build all tests and the freq_count program
make test       # build and run all unit tests
make memetest   # run all unit tests under valgrind (reports errors and memory leaks)
make clean      # remove all build products


To run freq_count on one or more text files:
./freq_coount file1.txt file2.txt


Overview of models:

Shared:
- common.h 
- defines elem_t union used for all key/value types

Hash table:
- hash_table.h hash_table.c hash_table_struct.h hash_table_tests.c
- maps elem_t keys to elem_t values

Hash table iterator:
- iterator.h iterator.c iterator_tests.c
- Visits every entry in the hash table once

Linked list:
- linked_list.h linked_list.c linked_list_struct.h linked_list_tests.c
- list of elem_t's along with functions to use on the list

List iterator:
- list_iterator.c list iterator.h list_iterator_tests.c
- Visits every element of the list in order

Application:
- freq_count.c
- Counts word frequencys in files using the hash table and hash table iterator

Design choices:

Genereic elements:
All containers (keys/values) stroes their values in union type elem_t. 
The user is responsible for reading the same field as was written to, 
since C has no runtime type information
(ex. int_elem(2) is read back with .i)

Hash Table:
The hash table is an array of buckets (No_buckets, currenty 17) each bucket
is a singly linked list wherre every first element is a sentinel node. 
The sentinel node removes the special case needed to handle empty buckets
and makes sure we never have to read from an empty bucket (that would be undefined behavior)

Linked list:
A singly linked list with a sentinel node first and pointers to the first and last link in the list.
Makes append, prepend and size O(1). 

Iterators:
The hash table iterator visits entries in no specific order, so code using the ht_iterator
must not depend on the order. The linked list iteration however visits the elemets in order

Failiure handling:
Functions that can not signal failiure through their return values use preconditions in their 
headers and assert statments in their implementation to crach the program if a precondition is violated




